    "attack_vector": "Expose the J-camp's arithmetic error regarding the terminal digits. Point out that all eight J-advocates mistakenly grouped (S, Z) together to claim the cadence fails, completely missing that P(16), Q(17), R(18), S(19) is a continuous four-term run of +1 in digital roots (7 -> 8 -> 9 -> 1). This proves the numerical design was meticulously engineered, which is impossible under J (where J=10 and L=12 breaks the run of pairs).",
    "target_colleagues": "Target Colleague 4 (who initially pursued mathematical/ASCII patterns) and Colleague 10 (who has been the most vocal about the 'apophenia' argument). If we demonstrate that their dismissal of the pattern was based on overlooking the 7-8-9-1 digital root progression, their intellectual confidence will be shaken.",
